From ec6cd5db141cfe6299e2e6ce544424a7a75d6259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanidhya Awasthi <sanidhya.awasthi@bfhl.in>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:14:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Skip overspent sources when a named cleanup pool collects
 funds

The end of month cleanup did not check whether a category set to send its
leftover funds to a named pool actually had a positive balance. An overspent
category was still processed, so its negative balance was budgeted back onto
itself and subtracted from the amount available to the pool, pushing the
overspending onto the other categories in the group.

Global sources already guard against this and warn instead. Apply the same
check to named pool sources so an overspent category is skipped and reported.

Closes #8739
